<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#game1> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "League of Legends (LoL), commonly referred to as League, is a 2009 multiplayer online battle arena video game developed and published by Riot Games. Inspired by Defense of the Ancients, a custom map for Warcraft III, Riot's founders sought to develop a stand-alone game in the same genre. Since its release in October 2009, League has been free-to-play and is monetized through purchasable character customization. The game is available for Microsoft Windows and macOS." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#game2> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "Dota 2 is a 2013 multiplayer online battle arena video game developed and published by Valve. The game is a sequel to Defense of the Ancients (DotA), which was a community-created mod for Blizzard Entertainment's Warcraft III: Reign of Chaos. Dota 2 is played in matches between two teams of five players, with each team occupying and defending their own separate base on the map. Available for Microsoft Windows, OS X, and Linux." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#game3> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "Heroes of the Storm (HotS) is a 2015 multiplayer online battle arena video game developed and published by Blizzard Entertainment. The game features various characters from Blizzard's franchises including Warcraft, Diablo, StarCraft, and Overwatch. Unlike other MOBAs, Heroes of the Storm focuses more on team play and objectives rather than individual player achievements. Available for Microsoft Windows and macOS." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#game4> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "Smite is a 2014 multiplayer online battle arena video game developed and published by Hi-Rez Studios. The game is unique in its use of a third-person perspective instead of the traditional top-down view. Players control a god, goddess, or other mythological figure and take part in team-based combat, using abilities and tactics against other player-controlled gods and NPC minions. Available for Microsoft Windows, macOS, PlayStation 4, Xbox One, and Nintendo Switch." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#game5> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "Vainglory is a 2014 multiplayer online battle arena video game developed and published by Super Evil Megacorp. The game was initially launched for iOS and later expanded to Android and PC platforms. Vainglory features a simplified control scheme suited for touchscreen devices and focuses on fast-paced, strategic gameplay. Available for iOS, Android, and Microsoft Windows." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Dota2> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "Dota 2 is a 2013 multiplayer online battle arena (MOBA) video game by Valve. The game is a sequel to Defense of the Ancients (DotA), a community-created mod for Blizzard Entertainment's Warcraft III: Reign of Chaos. Dota 2 is played in matches between two teams of five players, with each team occupying and defending their own separate base on the map. Each of the ten players independently controls a powerful character known as a \"hero\" that all have unique abilities and differing styles of play. During a match players collect experience points and items for their heroes to defeat the opposing team's heroes in player versus player combat. A team wins by being the first to destroy the other team's \"Ancient\", a large structure located within their base." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#LeagueOfLegends> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#gameDescription> "League of Legends (LoL), commonly referred to as League, is a 2009 multiplayer online battle arena video game developed and published by Riot Games. Inspired by Defense of the Ancients, a custom map for Warcraft III, Riot's founders sought to develop a stand-alone game in the same genre. Since its release in October 2009, League has been free-to-play and is monetized through purchasable character customization. The game is available for Microsoft Windows and macOS." .
