<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Shojin> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#itemEffect> "Dealing ability damage with a champion ability grants a stack for 6 seconds, stacking up to 4 times and up to 1 per cast instance per second and every second for damage over time abilities. For each stack, your ability damage and proc damage dealt by abilities gain 3% increased damage, for a total increase of 12% at maximum stacks." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#LongSword> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#itemEffect> "Long Sword is the basic item from which the gold value for the stat attack damage is derived (approximately 35 Gold 35 per point of attack damage)." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#CaulfieldWarhammer> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#itemEffect> "The Brutalizer's stats (old item that has been removed) has been split across two items. Its armor penetration went to Serrated Dirk Serrated Dirk and its cooldown reduction to Caulfield's Warhammer Caulfield's Warhammer." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Shojin> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#itemCost> "3100"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#CaulfieldWarhammer> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#itemCost> "1100"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#LongSword> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#itemCost> "350"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Bruiser> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#roleDescription> "Bruisers are a diverse group of short-ranged combatants who excel at both dealing and surviving damage. With easy access to heavy, continuous damage (or DPS) and a host of innate defenses, bruisers thrive in extended fights as they seek out enemies to take down, but their limited range puts them at constant risk of being kept at bay (or kited) by their opponents via crowd control, range and mobility." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Support> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#roleDescription> "The Support role is to aid and help protect your allies in any situation. Your role is is to shield or heal them, to tanking some damage or sacrificing yourself to keep others alive. You are often giving up the glorious kills in the game to support others, but in the end its usually the support to secure the true MVP award. Support heroes usually lane with the marksman in top lane or at mid lane in order to be able to travel quickly where they are needed." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Assassin> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#roleDescription> "An assassin is an agile hero that specializes in killing or disabling roaming targets picking them off as they try to replenish HP. Focused on infiltration, deception, and mobility, assassins are opportunistic hunters who find favorable moments within a fight before jumping into the fray. Regardless of the size of the enemy team, assassins specializes in positioning and artful killing." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Marksman> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#roleDescription> "Marksmen are ranged champions whose power almost exclusively revolves around their basic attacks: using their reach to land massive continuous damage from a distance, marksmen are capable of taking down even the toughest of opponents when positioned behind the safety of their team, and excel at securing map objectives." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Tank> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#roleDescription> "Tanks are tough melee champions who sacrifice damage in exchange for powerful crowd control. While able to engage enemies in combat, a tank's purpose isn't usually to kill opponents; rather, tanks excel at disrupting enemies and diverting focus to themselves, allowing them to lock down specific targets (or several targets at once), as well as remove (or peel) threats from their allies." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Mage> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#roleDescription> "Mages are champions who typically possess great reach, ability-based area of effect damage and crowd control, and who use all of these strengths in tandem with each other to trap and destroy enemies from a distance. Specializing in magic damage, often burst damage, and therefore investing heavily in items that allow them to cast stronger and faster spells, mages excel at chaining their abilities together in powerful combos in order to win fights, though their abilities also tend to be difficult to land and can be mitigated, if not avoided completely, by their targets if they react in time." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#OceanDrake> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Ocean Drake is an epic jungle dragon that requires a group to defeat. It attacks with blows that deal moderate damage, but its buff is continuous regeneration of health and mana. It is a crucial objective for teams aiming to maintain pressure and sustainability in the match." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#RedBrambleback> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Red Brambleback, known as Krug, is a neutral monster found in the red jungle. When attacked, it inflicts heavy damage with periodic attacks. Near death, it explodes into a damaging thorn cloud for enemies. Crucial for jungle efficiency in controlling the red jungle." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#InfernalDrake> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Infernal Drake is an epic jungle dragon that requires a group to defeat. It attacks with powerful blows that deal attack and magic damage. It is a strategic objective in the jungle, favoring aggressive and combat-oriented gameplay." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SiegeMinion> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Siege Minion is one of three minion types appearing in each wave. It attacks from long range with powerful shots that deal significant damage to enemy structures. It has the highest resilience among minions, crucial for assaulting enemy bastions." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#CasterMinion> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Caster Minion is one of three minion types appearing in each wave. It attacks at range with magic attacks that deal moderate but continuous damage. It has lower resilience but higher potential damage compared to the Melee Minion." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#MeleeMinion> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Melee Minion is one of three minion types appearing in each wave. It attacks melee with modest damage but has higher resilience compared to other minion types. Designed to advance against enemy defenses and support allied champions." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#BlueSentinel> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Blue Sentinel, also known as Gromp, is a neutral monster residing in the blue jungle. When attacked, it deals periodic damage and increases attack speed as its health decreases. Strategically positioned to encourage advancement for champions controlling the blue jungle." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SuperMinion> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureDescription> "The Super Minion is a special type of minion appearing in the lane where the enemy inhibitor has been destroyed. It has high resilience and deals significant damage to structures and enemy champions. It represents a major threat and requires a quick response from the opposing team." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Blind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Mechanic> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#PickAndBan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#Mechanic> .
