<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SummonerRiftMidLane> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#laneDescription> "The mid lane is located centrally on the map, directly connecting the bases of both teams. It is typically the shortest path among the three main lanes and often serves as the focal point for combat actions and strategic movements. The mid lane is usually dominated by magic-based champions or assassins who can deal high burst damage quickly. This lane is crucial for controlling game flow and supporting other lanes with swift movements and targeted attacks." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SummonerRiftJungle> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#laneDescription> "The jungle consists of the parts of the map between the lanes proper, excluding the teams' bases, characterized by the lack of vision or dense Fog of War. Neutral—not aggressive unless attacked—creeps called Monster icon monsters live in the jungle, and a monster or group of monsters at a certain location of the map is called a camp." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SummonerRiftBotLane> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#laneDescription> "The bot lane is situated at the bottom of the map, parallel to the top lane. It is a strategic environment that involves cooperation between two players, typically an ADC (Attack Damage Carry) and a support. This lane features a combination of defensive towers and enemy attacks, making it critical for map control and protecting the elemental dragon in the lower jungle." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SummonerRiftTopLane> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#laneDescription> "The top lane is one of the three main paths on the map, situated at the top relative to each team's base. It is characterized by a long, narrow terrain with towers positioned to defend access to the base. The top lane is known for being a battleground for durable champions and melee fighters. Common champions in this lane include fighters or tanks, capable of enduring heavy damage and engaging in direct combat." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#LoLItalianTournamentSpring2024> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#isOfficialCompetition> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#WorldChampionship2023> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#isOfficialCompetition> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#NorthAmericanChallengersLeagueSummer2024> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#isOfficialCompetition> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#SummonerRift> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#mapGameplay> "The objective of Summoner's Rift is simple – destroy the enemy nexus. In order to do this, champions must traverse down one of three different paths (or lanes) in order to attack their enemy at their weakest points they can exploit. Both teams have their lanes defended by numerous turrets; each turret grows in strength the closer it gets to its respective nexus and each turret must be eliminated in order to gain access to the next turret in that lane. Cooperating with fellow summoners is an absolute requirement for success, as it is easy for a champion to find themselves ambushed by enemies in the lanes of the Rift." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#RedBrambleback> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureHasBuff> "Burn Damage and Slow" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#InfernalDrake> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureHasBuff> "Infernal Buff (Increased Attack Damage and Ability Power)" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#BlueSentinel> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureHasBuff> "Mana Regeneration" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#OceanDrake> <http://www.semanticweb.org/MobaOntology#creatureHasBuff> "Ocean Buff (Regeneration of Health and Mana)" .
